                         [--chunk K] [--json] [--self-test]

Print the manifest, function-context diff, hunk ranges, and pre-merge-base
history for one target's changes. With --store, persist the complete context
privately and bound each call's diff output; with --from, read bounded chunks
back from that store without touching git.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --merge-base MERGE_BASE
                        the pinned merge-base SHA
  --head HEAD           the pinned head SHA
  --worktree            snapshot working files before building context
  --parent PARENT       prior worktree snapshot; chain only while source HEAD
                        is unchanged
  --prior-head PRIOR_HEAD
                        the head the earlier review pinned; adds the delta
                        sections
  --base-ref BASE_REF   the base branch (e.g. origin/main) that decides merge-
                        base-unchanged
  --path PATH           repo-relative path to select, literally; repeatable;
                        --path=PATH for a leading dash
  --store FILE          persist the complete context to this private file and
                        bound the output
  --chunk-bytes N       the byte bound a stored call's diff text must fit; the
                        build call charges its other sections against it first
                        (default 24000). Only used with --store: the bound is
                        fixed when the store is written
  --from FILE           read from a store written by --store instead of git;
                        never rebuilds the diff
  --section {diff,delta-diff}
                        which diff a --from read comes from (default diff)
  --chunk K             with --from and one --path: print chunk K of that path
                        (1-based)
  --json                emit one JSON object instead of Markdown
  --self-test           check the command against a scratch repository

Selection and recovery: --path P (repeatable, literal, use --path=P for a
leading dash) limits the diff and delta-diff output; --store FILE writes the
complete context and prints at most --chunk-bytes of diff per call; --from
FILE [--section diff|delta-diff] --path P [--chunk K] prints one path or one
chunk from the store and marks it consumed in the `## chunks` inventory. Exit
2 names an unknown path, an out-of-range chunk, or an unreadable store.
